[[:db/retract 17592186134407 :question/answer-fields 17592186132481] {:db/id 17592186329653 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 8 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{6} & 9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 4 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nConsider the matrix given above. Identify **all** of the reasons why one can conclude that $|A|=0?$\n\nI. $A$ has proportional rows\n\nII. $A$ has identical columns\n\nIII. $A$ has a zero column" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134414 :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $|A|=0.$ Which of the following statements must be true?\n\nI. $A$ has two identical rows\n\nII. One of the rows/columns of $A$ is proportional to another row/column of $A$\n\nIII. $A$ has two identical columns" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133911 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-df55035e-2530-507b-9e8e-793ed8f0bafc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-df55035e-2530-507b-9e8e-793ed8f0bafc" :question/id #uuid "df55035e-2530-507b-9e8e-793ed8f0bafc" :question/math-academy-id "q-82284" :question/problem "Find $-4det(A)+3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\ndet(B)=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3=6\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-4det(A)+3det(B)=-4\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 6=18.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-25bbbab1-f79f-5a4a-95b4-1d90cbb77585"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-25bbbab1-f79f-5a4a-95b4-1d90cbb7758